<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Forvia's brand mark, as a native vector — same path data as the web app's
  components/LogoMark.jsx (vectorized once, from the real logo, via potrace). Kept in this same
  potrace-native coordinate space (0..~3200) with a group transform to flip/scale it into the
  320x313 viewport, exactly mirroring the SVG's own `translate(0,313) scale(0.1,-0.1)` — so this
  file and LogoMark.jsx's path strings can be diffed/copied directly if the mark ever changes.

  Each path starts fully hidden (trimPathEnd="0", fillAlpha="0") — see
  ic_forvia_logo_animated.xml, which is what SplashActivity actually shows: it strokes each
  path in (a native "draw the outline" — trimPathEnd is Android's own version of the web's
  stroke-dasharray/dashoffset trick), then cross-fades stroke to fill, same two-stage reveal
  as the web boot screen.
-->
